  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a sequence A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ which contains pairwise distinct elements and a sequence B1,B2,…,BNB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_NB1​,B2​,…,BN​, which also contains pairwise distinct elements (but not necessarily distinct from elements of AAA). For each valid iii, 1≤Ai,Bi≤2⋅N1 \\leq A_i, B_i \\leq 2 \\cdot N1≤Ai​,Bi​≤2⋅N.\n\nYou may rotate BBB as many times as you want. A rotation consists of moving the first element of the sequence to the end. Afterwards, let's define a sequence C1,C2,…,CNC_1, C_2, \\ldots, C_NC1​,C2​,…,CN​ as Ci=(Ai+Bi)%NC_i = (A_i + B_i) \\% NCi​=(Ai​+Bi​)%N for each valid iii.\n\nThere are NNN possible sequences CCC. Find the lexicographically smallest of these sequences.\n\n**Note:** A sequence xxx is lexicographically smaller than a different sequence yyy if xi &lt; yix_i &lt; y_ixi​ &lt; yi​, where iii is the smallest valid index where the sequences xxx and yyy differ.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\nThe third line contains NNN space-separated integers B1,B2,…,BNB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_NB1​,B2​,…,BN​.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print a single line containing NNN space-separated integers C1,C2,…,CNC_1, C_2, \\ldots, C_NC1​,C2​,…,CN​ denoting the lexicographically smallest sequence.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\leq T \\leq 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤Ai,Bi≤2⋅N1 \\leq A_i, B_i \\leq 2 \\cdot N1≤Ai​,Bi​≤2⋅N for each valid iii",
      "the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask #1 (100 points):** original constraints"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
